schema: "0.4"
id: cockpit-17-cloud-sync-and-account
type: image
quality: high

# The Robot Learns — a terminal-native personal knowledge base (CLI, no web UI) — Cloud Sync & Account.
# Theme tenets (Cockpit): cool graphite panes divided by box-drawing rules, ONE electric-magenta signal for
#   selection/focus, disciplined four-color status set, mono data + tight grotesk labels, radius 0-1px, flat.
# Palette (do NOT write these hex into prompt.text): canvas #0e1116, ink #c9d1d9, active-pane #161b22,
#   dim border #30363d, magenta accent #ff2e88; status green #3fb950 / amber #d29922 / red #f85149 / blue #58a6ff.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity mockup of a dense TERMINAL user
    interface (TUI) — a modern "mission control" console in the lineage of k9s, btop, and lazygit.
    This is rendered INSIDE a terminal window: no browser chrome, no marketing whitespace, no rounded
    cards, no drop shadows. Cool blue-graphite panes divided by thin box-drawing rules; a SINGLE
    electric-magenta signal marks the active pane and the selected conflict; status uses a rationed
    four-color set (green, amber, red, blue), each with a glyph. Monospaced data + a tight grotesk for
    titles/labels only. The signature element here is a two-column diff/merge conflict resolver.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity screenshot of a dense terminal-UI (TUI) console filling the whole frame, the
    "Cloud Sync & Account" screen of a terminal knowledge-base tool. Cool dark blue-graphite
    background; crisp box-drawn panes; monospaced text; NOT a web page.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (top sync-status strip + a dominant diff resolver + a right status pane + footer):
    - TOP "SYNC STATUS" STRIP: account identity "acct: maya@team", a last-sync marker "synced 6m ago",
      and up/down transfer counts with arrows "↑ 12  ↓ 3", plus an active tab among
      "[sync] [conflicts] [team] [account]" with a magenta underline.
    - CENTER PANE "MERGE CONFLICTS" (dominant, the ACTIVE pane — electric-magenta border,
      one-step-lighter fill): an item-by-item diff/merge conflict resolver laid out as TWO side-by-side
      mono columns headed "LOCAL" and "REMOTE", separated by a box-drawing rule. Each conflict is a
      pair of rows showing the same article key with differing fields; removed/changed lines are marked
      with leading - and + gutters (red - for local-only, green + for remote-only). ONE conflict is
      selected — a magenta left-edge bar and a highlighted band across both columns — with an inline
      choice row beneath it: "[l]keep local  [r]keep remote  [b]keep both  [e]edit". ~3 conflicts stacked.
    - RIGHT PANE "SYNC" (~28%): compact key:value status readouts with glyphs — "synced   ✓ 1,204",
      "pending  ⟳ 15", "conflicts ! 3", "shared KB  team-ml" — and a small block meter for upload
      progress "▇▇▇▇▅░░ 71%". This pane is inactive (dim graphite border).
    - BOTTOM KEYBIND FOOTER: a persistent dim row —
      "[n]next-conflict  [l/r/b]resolve  [s]sync-now  [tab]pane  :cmd  ?help".

    PALETTE & TYPE: cool blue-graphite neutrals everywhere (never warm gray), cool off-white ink for
    data; the ONLY saturated brand hue is the electric magenta on the active-pane border, the selected
    conflict bar and the active tab. Diff gutters and sync status use signal green / amber / red / blue,
    each with a glyph — the magenta selection is never confused with red error because selection also
    carries the edge bar. Monospaced tabular figures align both diff columns; titles and labels are a
    tight grotesk small-caps.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: crisp rectangles, radius 0-1px, no rounded cards, no pills, no drop shadows; flat
    tonal depth from box-drawing rules and the one-step-lighter active tone only.

    MOOD: a professional instrument panel for reconciling a synced knowledge base — measured,
    disciplined, current; dense, cool, awake.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, browser window chrome, rounded cards, drop shadows, marketing hero whitespace, blurry, distorted UI"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches the screen: a sync-status strip with account and transfer counts, a two-column LOCAL/REMOTE diff-merge conflict resolver with per-item resolve choices, a sync-status readout pane"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Cool graphite TUI with box-drawing panes, single magenta signal on active pane/selected conflict, four-color status+diff with glyphs, mono data + grotesk labels, radius 0-1, no shadows"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Dense multi-pane terminal layout dominated by the diff resolver, clear hierarchy, plausible real TUI; persistent keybind footer"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9, terminal window (no browser chrome), no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "rendered as a web page / browser instead of a terminal window"

tags: [cockpit, therobotlearns.com, screen-mockup]
